    "Description": ".NET is a fast, lightweight and modular platform for creating cross platform applications that work on Linux, macOS and Windows.  It particularly focuses on creating console applications, web applications and micro-services.  .NET contains a runtime conforming to .NET Standards a set of framework libraries, an SDK containing compilers and a 'dotnet' application to drive everything.\n\nBug Fix(es):\n\n* Update .NET 6.0 to SDK 6.0.135 and Runtime 6.0.35 [rhel-9.5.z] (JIRA:RHEL-60799)Bug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Update .NET 6.0 to SDK 6.0.135 and Runtime 6.0.35 [rhel-9.5.z] (JIRA:RHEL-60799)\n\n* dotnet6.0: Multiple .NET components susceptible to hash flooding [rhel-9.5] (JIRA:RHEL-60992)\n\n* dotnet6.0: Denial of Service in System.Text.Json [rhel-9.5] (JIRA:RHEL-61010)\n\n* dotnet6.0: System.IO.Packaging - Multiple DoS vectors in use of SortedList [rhel-9.5] (JIRA:RHEL-61014)\n\n* dotnet6.0: nodejs-ws: denial of service when handling a request with many HTTP headers [rhel-9] (JIRA:RHEL-43154)",
